OL,1,Vk4                               G2/9
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGCISKEI LEADER
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGDEFIES ANC
OL,4,D
OL,5, Brigadier Oupa Gqozo says he will not
OL,6, resign and will not accede to demands
OL,7, for a referendum following the massacre
OL,8, of 28 ANC protesters yesterday.
OL,9,F
OL,10,FHe told the BBC that his troops opened
OL,11,Ffire after one of them was shot dead,
OL,12,Fand had acted with some restraint.
OL,13,F
OL,14,FMeanwhile, the South African Law and
OL,15,FOrder Ministry has criticised the ANC
OL,16,Ffor its part in the Siskei massacre.
OL,18,FThe demonstration was not a spontaneous
OL,19,Foutburst of democratic rage but part of
OL,20,Fthe ANC's programme of action, it said.
OL,21,F
OL,22,D]F This Ceefax page is fromG08-09-92
OL,23,D] FMuch more at: teletextarchive.com
