PN,18103
SC,0003
CT,8,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F181A1788899632
OL,1,Vk4                               G3/9
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGMANDELA DEMANDS INQUIRY
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGINTO CISKEI MASSACRE
OL,4,D
OL,5, ANC leader Nelson Mandela has called
OL,6, for a full investigation into the
OL,7, massacre of 28 protesters in the South
OL,8, African homeland of Ciskei.
OL,10,FLaying a wreath at the site of the
OL,11,Fkillings, he demanded the immediate
OL,12,Fremoval of Ciskei's leader Oupa Gqozo.
OL,14,FIn a bitter attack, Mr Mandela accused
OL,15,FPresident de Klerk of soliciting his
OL,16,Fhis cooperation "whilst he was busy
OL,17,Fpreparing for war against the people".
OL,19,FEarlier, Archbishop Desmond Tutu put a
OL,20,Fplan for a referendum to Ciskei's
OL,21,Fleadership to defuse the crisis.
OL,22,F
OL,23,D]FFromG08-09-92F  teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,182,180,120,250,0,100
PN,18104
