OL,1,Vk4                               G6/9
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGTWO FRENCH UN SOLDIERS
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGKILLED IN SARAJEVO
OL,5, Two French UN soldiers were killed when
OL,6, a UN convoy was hit by machinegun fire
OL,7, near Sarajevo airport this evening.
OL,8,F
OL,9,FA spokesman said the convoy was hit
OL,10,Fafter a long drive from Belgrade and it
OL,11,Fwas unclear who opened fire, raising
OL,12,Fthe death toll among UN troops in
OL,13,FBosnia to four with 46 wounded.
OL,14,F
OL,15,FEarlier, Bosnian Serb leader Radovan
OL,16,FKaradzic did not make it clear whether
OL,17,Fhis forces would abide by a deadline
OL,18,Fset for UN control of heavy weapons.
OL,20,FEC peace negotiator Lord Owen is
OL,21,Fexpected to visit Sarajevo tomorrow.
OL,22,F
OL,23,D]FFromG08-09-92F  teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
