OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F181A1788899632
OL,1,Vk4                               G7/9
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGMORE ARRESTS LIKELY AFTER
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGCOUNTERFEITING RAIDS
OL,4,F
OL,5, Armed police took part in a major swoop
OL,6, against organised crime in southern
OL,7, England today; 27 people were arrested.
OL,9,FMore than #1.5m in forged currency was
OL,10,Fseized, together with forged documents,
OL,11,Fover 40 guns, plastic explosives and
OL,12,Fstolen cars.
OL,13,F
OL,14,FThe raids were the climax of a probe
OL,15,Finto a "quartermaster" service
OL,16,Fsupplying criminals with the tools of
OL,17,Ftheir trade.
OL,19,FThe raids, codenamed Mensa, involved
OL,20,Fmore than 100 police officers in Devon,
OL,21,FDorset, London and the Home Counties.
OL,22,F
OL,23,D]FFromG08-09-92F  teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
