OL,1,Vk4                               G8/9
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGMAJOR WELCOMES MIDDLE
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGEAST PEACE TALKS
OL,4,D
OL,5, Prime Minister John Major told Israeli
OL,6, foreign minister Shimon Peres that
OL,7, Europe would do whatever it could to
OL,8, speed up the Middle East peace process.
OL,10,FMr Major, the current European
OL,11,FCommmunity president, said: "The two
OL,12,Fsides are now sitting down and talking.
OL,13,FThat is a credit to both sides."
OL,14,F
OL,15,FHe added that there would be occasional
OL,16,F"difficulties, hitches and setbacks",
OL,17,Fbut it was essential that the
OL,18,FArab-Israeli talks continued.
OL,19,F
OL,20,F"I believe there is a will there to
OL,21,Fcontinue those talks," he said.
OL,22,F
OL,23,D]FFromG08-09-92F  teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
